  "answer_text": "The evidence provided does not contain sufficient data to determine which method achieves the lowest hallucination rate within each paper. While several papers report hallucination metrics (e.g., hallucination rate, hallucination frequency, unsupported-answer rate), the specific numerical values for all compared methods are missing from the provided passages. In the few instances where results are tabulated, the value for the retrieval-augmented method is often listed as \"see text\" rather than a number, or the table only provides data for a subset of the methods described in the Method section. For example, in [S084, 720-2103], the RAG pipeline's hallucination rate is listed as \"see text\" while the vanilla LLM is 18.9%, and in [S088, 763-2152], the RAG pipeline's hallucination frequency is \"see text\" while the vanilla LLM is 31.7%. Without the full numerical results for all methods in each paper, it is impossible to identify the method with the lowest rate for every paper.",
